{"name":"Esplanade","hex":"#d5bda4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"esplanade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clear space between a citadel and the nearest houses of the town.","The glacis of the counterscarp, or the slope of the parapet of the covered way toward the country."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/esplanade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Esplanade","blocks":[{"text":"An esplanade or promenade is a long, open, level area, usually next to a river or large body of water, where people may walk. The historical definition of esplanade was a large, open, level area outside fortress or city walls to provide clear fields of fire for the fortress's guns. In modern usage, the space allows the area to be paved as a pedestrian walk; esplanades are often on sea fronts and allow walking whatever the state of the tide, without having to walk on the beach."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Atlantic_City_Boardwalk_view_north_from_Caesars_Atlantic_City_by_Silveira_Neto_June_24_2012.jpg/330px-Atlantic_City_Boardwalk_view_north_from_Caesars_Atlantic_City_by_Silveira_Neto_June_24_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esplanade"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Central_City_Park%2C_May_Day%2C_1876_-_DPLA_-_b42178cb2f6ff2dfd3c7d07b805cd814.jpeg/500px-Central_City_Park%2C_May_Day%2C_1876_-_DPLA_-_b42178cb2f6ff2dfd3c7d07b805cd814.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Central_City_Park%2C_May_Day%2C_1876_-_DPLA_-_b42178cb2f6ff2dfd3c7d07b805cd814.jpeg/500px-Central_City_Park%2C_May_Day%2C_1876_-_DPLA_-_b42178cb2f6ff2dfd3c7d07b805cd814.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Central City Park, Macon, GA; May Day, 1876","link":"http